# bat configuration. One command-line argument per line.
#
# The carbonfox theme is a .tmTheme (Sublime/TextMate format) shipped in
# themes/ next to this file. It must be compiled into bat's cache before it
# resolves -- see the package README:
#
#     bat cache --build     # 'batcat' on Debian/Ubuntu
#
# git-delta reads bat's theme registry, so building the cache also makes
# `syntax-theme = carbonfox` work in ~/.gitconfig.

--theme="carbonfox"

# Show line numbers and git modification markers, but no heavy box drawing.
--style="numbers,changes,header"

# Keep bat's output in the terminal when it fits on one screen.
--paging=auto
